          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em dg-module
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            is the specialization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monoid"} module over a monoid
            to the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebras"} dg-algebras
            with many objects, i.e.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-categories"} dg-categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#over_dgalgebras Over dg-algebras
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            in an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            with respect to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A left (resp. right)
              %strong dg-module
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a left (resp. right)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monoid"} module
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p Spelling this out in components, it means the following:
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-module"} dg-module
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho \;\colon\; A \otimes V \longrightarrow V
            %p
              out of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              property. Explicitly this means that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                  preserves degrees: for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
                  of homogeneous degrees
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert a \vert}
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert v \vert}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo +
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert \rho(a,v)\vert = {\vert a \vert} + {\vert v \vert}
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  in degree
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert a \vert
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi A
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi V
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d_V (\rho(a,v)) = \rho(d_A a, v) + (-1)^{\vert a\vert} \rho(a,d_V v)
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in A
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\rho(a,\rho(b,v)) = \rho(a \cdot b,v)
                        \\,.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V_i, \rho_i)
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              between them is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \;\colon\; V_1 \longrightarrow V_2
            %p
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho_2(a, \phi(v)) = \phi(\rho_1(a,v))
                    \\,.
            %p
              This defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              We say that a morphism of dg-modules is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
              if its underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
              is, hence if it induces an isomorphism on
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod
              a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
          %h3#over_dgcategories Over dg-categories
          %p
            More generally let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A left (resp. right)
              %strong dg-module
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+an+enriched+category"} module
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              in the sense of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-categories"} dg-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi dg
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi mod
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M : T^{op} \longrightarrow dg-mod_k
            %p
              (resp.
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi dg
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi mod
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M : T \longrightarrow dg-mod_k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is the base
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
          %p
            Note that when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
            with a single object, a dg-module over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the same thing as a dg-module over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphisms"} endomorphisms
            of the unique object.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong shift
              of a dg-module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              by an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is the dg-module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M[n]
              defined by composing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              with the shift
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -[n]
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dg
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi mod
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dg-mod_k
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            By general
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-category"} dg-category
            which we denote
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dg
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi mod
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dg-mod_T
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A dg-module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dg
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi mod
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \in dg-mod_T
              is called
              %strong representable
              if it is in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Yoneda+embedding"} dg-Yoneda embedding
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is called
              %strong free
              if it is equivalent to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of shifts of representable dg-modules.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is called
              %strong semi-free
              if it admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtration"} filtration
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded+objects"} associated graded objects
              are free dg-modules.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+dg-module"} minimal dg-module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-comodule"} dg-comodule
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"}> Bertrand Toen
              , section 3 in
              = succeed "," do
                %em The homotopy theory of dg-categories and derived Morita theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0408337"} arXiv:math/0408337
          %p Paragraph 2.2 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Orlov"}> Dmitri Orlov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Smooth and proper noncommutative schemes and gluing of DG categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1402.7364"} arXiv:1402.7364
